<section class="shell band faq">
  <h2>Questions about walk and talk therapy</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>What is walk and talk therapy?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>A therapy session held outdoors while walking, rather than seated in an office or on
      video. The clinical work is the same and the confidentiality obligations are the same;
      the setting changes the pressure of the conversation and gives the body something to
      do.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>How much does a walk therapy session cost?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>$125 for a one-hour session. It
      is paid in advance to hold the spot, with no refunds for cancellations inside 48 hours.
      Regular 50-minute online sessions with Reem are $240.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Can I start with a walk session?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>No. Walk, movement and equine sessions begin after a free consult and one to three
      online sessions, so the pacing and the working relationship are established before the
      setting changes.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>How is privacy handled outdoors?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Your confidentiality is maintained outdoors just as it is indoors. Because a trail is
      public, that is a planning question rather than an afterthought: route and timing, how
      conversation is handled when someone passes, and what you would want to do if you saw
      someone you know. All of it is agreed before the first walk.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Where do the walk sessions happen?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>On trails in central Texas, on Fridays. The specific location is arranged with you,
      and the equine sessions are near Dripping Springs.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Is walk and talk therapy available for teenagers?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>No. Trail walk, movement and equine sessions are for adults 18 and over. The practice
      sees adults and young adults, including college-age clients, for online therapy, and does
      not work with young children.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
